# PXD014739 — Arabidopsis histone PTM reference workflow

## Dataset

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| PRIDE accession | PXD014739 |
| Organism | *Arabidopsis thaliana* (Col-0) |
| Sample | Acid-extracted histones, propionylated |
| Acquisition | DDA (data-dependent) |
| Instrument | LTQ Orbitrap Elite hybrid (Thermo Fisher Scientific) |
| Injections | 114 (genetic arm: 6 plants x 3 injections per genotype; chemical arm: NaB and TSA) |

## Files in this directory

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `histone_ratios_PXD014739.xls` | Cohort-level PTM ratio table (OutputTogether output) |
| `PXD014739_XIC_gallery_subset_cropped.pdf` | Representative XIC traces for selected peptides |
| `paper_PXD014739.pdf` | Associated publication (open access) |

## How to reproduce

```matlab
% 1. Download RAW files from PRIDE: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pride/archive/projects/PXD014739
% 2. Place them in a folder (e.g., data/PXD014739/)
% 3. Run the AT bundle:
cd bundles/AT/src
EpiProfile
% 4. When prompted, point to the RAW folder
% 5. Output appears in data/PXD014739/histone_layouts/
```

## Parameters used

- Mass tolerance: 10 ppm (default, set in `check_otherparas.m`)
- Debug mode: off (`ndebug = 0`)
- Figures: enabled (`nfigure = 1`)

## Provenance and validation (2026-08-15)

`histone_ratios_PXD014739.xls` holds 114 sample columns and 115 data rows (87 map to the
peptidoform catalogue, 21 are sequence variants). SHA-256 starts with `793b83a60bb5df3b`.
Intensity profile: areas from 413 to 2.33e10, none above 1e12, 72.1 % of ratios positive,
median RT 36.97 min. This is the copy the Chapter 4 atlas ingests.

Cross-checked against a re-extraction of 11 *hda6-6* runs produced with `RawToMS1.exe` on
2026-08-15: Pearson r = 0.9999 over 935 positive ratio pairs, median |delta ratio| 0.0001,
median RT difference 0.000 min, detection 0.741 vs 0.742. The quantification in this file is
sound.

**Do not confuse this file with the quantification under `E:\epiprofile_data\PXD014739\`**, now
renamed `histone_ratios_CORRUPTO_xtract_NO_USAR.xls`. That one was produced from `.MS1` files
generated with `xtract` 3.0.0 instead of `RawToMS1.exe`, which overflows the areas (median
1.43e38, maximum 8.40e61) and drops detection to 10.2 %. See
`crosstool_h3h4_bench_AT\docs\HALLAZGO_MS1_ELITE.md` for the full diagnosis.

## When this file was produced

Upper bound: it was already in the initial commit of this repository, `5f0085f`, dated
2026-02-20 14:02. The XIC gallery in this same directory is a ReportLab render of the per-region
PDFs of that run, and its metadata gives **2026-02-05 10:03:21 UTC**, so the run predates that
date. The module set also fits: 11 H3 and H4 modules, no H1, H2A or H2B, and the expanded bundle
only landed on 2026-03-27 (`1aef69f`, `3307eba`).

The run predates the extractor failure. `D:\epiprofile_data\convert_and_extract.py`, dated
2026-02-19 19:43, is what routed `.ms1` extraction through `xtract_xml.exe`
(`D:\EpiProfile2.1_1Basic_Running_version\`, product version **3.0.0.0**), and the broken `.MS1`
files carry a timestamp of 2026-02-19 21:56, two hours later and two weeks after the gallery.

Open caveat: no artefact of the original run survives. No `histone_layouts` directory, no
`histone_logs.txt`, no `paras.txt`, no intermediate `.mat` for this cohort predates 2026-02-20
anywhere on `D:` or `E:`. Four byte-identical copies of the `.xls` exist and none carries an
execution log. The numbers are validated, the provenance is not.
